sections.raw_text:
Upon completion of the Programme, students will have:
(1)
acquired the ability to apply knowledge of engineering sciences and mathematics to the discipline of mechanical and automation engineering;
(2)
acquired the ability to design and conduct experiments, as well as to analyze and interpret the data obtained;
(3)
acquired the ability to design a system, component, or process to meet desired needs within social, environmental and technical constraints;
(4)
acquired the ability to function on teams;
(5)
acquired the ability to identify, formulate, and solve engineering problems;
(6)
acquired the recognition of professional and ethical responsibility;
(7)
acquired the ability to communicate effectively;
(8)
acquired the ability to understand the impact of engineering solutions in a global and societal context, especially the importance of health, safety and environmental considerations to both workers and the general public;
(9)
acquired the ability to stay abreast of contemporary issues;
(10)
acquired the ability to recognize the need for and to engage in life-long learning;
(11)
acquired the ability to use the techniques, skills and tools to practice in the mechanical and automation engineering discipline; and
(12)
acquired the ability to use the computer/IT tools relevant to the discipline along with an understanding of their processes and limitations.
